WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.720
<v The First AD>Book eighteen. Odysseus drops Irus. Beggars, to your marks.

2
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.000
<v The Director>Which one is Irus?

3
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.030
<v The First AD>Irus is the one on the left.

4
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.400
<v Irus>I'm on the right.

5
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.250
<v Odysseus>I am the unknown beggar.

6
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:26.080
<v The Cinematographer>Same head. Same grey beard. Same rags, same staff. Part for part, and colour for colour.

7
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.170
<v The Director>Wardrobe.

8
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.920
<v The First AD>He means: can we tell them apart?

9
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:34.610
<v The Cinematographer>The camera note says: hard to tell apart.

10
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.060
<v The First AD>Noted. Still wrong.

11
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:42.090
<v The First AD>Book seventeen. Antinous throws the stool. Take two.

12
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:44.680
<v Antinous>Which beggar?

13
00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.110
<v The First AD>The one who isn't Irus.

14
00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.000
<v Antinous>Which one is Irus?

15
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.010
<v The Director>Action.

16
00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.090
<v The Director>Was that it?

17
00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.340
<v The Cinematographer>A third of a second. And it landed outside the frame.

18
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.280
<v The First AD>The experiment. A stool reads as thrown if it is in the air for more than half a second.

19
00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:15.210
<v The Cinematographer>The variable: the flight, a third of a second to six tenths. And smear bricks.

20
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.980
<v The Director>Smear?

21
00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:24.830
<v The Cinematographer>For two drawings the stool is drawn long, in bricks, along its path. The LEGO Movie does it. No blur.

22
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.780
<v The First AD>Held: the voices, the blocking, the lenses. Take three.

23
00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:31.490
<v The Director>Action.

24
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.270
<v Odysseus>I stand like a rock. It's in the book.

25
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.600
<v The Director>Was that it?

26
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.930
<v The Cinematographer>Six tenths of a second.

27
00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:48.830
<v The Director>Print it.

28
00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.780
<v Irus>Do I get a stool?

29
00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:54.390
<v The First AD>You get dropped. Next week.
